# p_4e7a — Keys and Coats Stay Home: The Entry Holds the Week

The per-object evidence is unambiguous: on weekdays between 9:00 and 17:00, Yuki's keys are found at the entry table four out of four times, and Marco's keys are found at the entry floor two out of four times (the other two looks being empty, consistent with him carrying them while in the kitchen). Neither set of keys is out of the house during this window. Yuki's jacket sits on the entry hook, not the entry floor as p_a1b2 predicts; her shoes are at the shoe rack, not the entry floor. Marco's jacket, backpack, water bottle, and notebook all rest on the entry hook. The dog leash is at the entry hook, found four out of four times in the 9-17h window.

This document directly contradicts the top-weighted hypotheses that send Yuki's keys out of the house in the afternoon (p_a1b2, p_c3d4, p_e5f6, p_7890, p_c9d4). The resident sightings confirm Yuki is in the house all day (bedroom at night, living at 8:00, kitchen 10:00–20:00), so she has no reason to take her keys out. Marco is in the kitchen at 10:00 and 12:00, then gone by 14:00; his keys likely travel with him only after 13:00.

What would refute this document: a look at the entry table during 9-17h that finds Yuki's keys missing, or a look at the entry floor that finds Marco's keys missing on a weekday morning when he is still home.

