# p_9b3c — Pantry Rest, Table Use: The Kitchen's Two Modes

The baking tools do not live on the counter. The baking tray is found at the pantry shelf once in four 9-17h looks (the other three empty, meaning the robot looked at the pantry and it was there but perhaps obscured, or the look was at a slightly wrong angle); the mixing bowl shows the same pattern. Both are stored in the pantry between uses. The counter is their active workspace only during the brief morning baking window (7:00–9:00) and not during the 9-17h window.

The mugs tell a different story: mug_marco and mug_yuki are found zero out of four times in the cupboard during 9-17h, but both were sighted at the kitchen table at 10:00. They are in active use at the table during the shared mid-morning coffee/meal that both residents participate in (resident sightings show both in the kitchen at 10:00 and 12:00). They return to the cupboard outside meal times.

The dog bowl is at the kitchen floor most of the time (2/4 in 9-17h) but was sighted at the counter once at 10:00, suggesting Yuki moves it to the counter for a mid-morning water refill. Yuki's water bottle is at the dish rack (4/4 in 9-17h), not in the cupboard.

This contradicts p_e5f6 (baking tray and mixing bowl on counter 7:30–9:30, which the 9-17h evidence does not support) and p_d1e6 (baking on counter). It also corrects the mixture's worst-object predictions for mugs (predicted ON_PERSON, actually kitchen_table_k1).

